WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
How do you watch living synapses learn while controlling their chemistry?

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.400
Inside an intact brain, deep circuits are hard to reach and hard to bathe in drugs.

3
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.100
Keep a thin brain slice alive in a dish, and the local circuit keeps working.

4
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.620
Much of this work uses rat hippocampus, a brain region wired as three relays.

5
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.440
The perforant path feeds dentate gyrus, and mossy fibres feed CA3.

6
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.880
Schaffer collaterals feed CA1 inside the neuropil, the mesh of fibers where synapses

7
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.880
lie.

8
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.090
Stimulate Schaffer collaterals to release glutamate, the main excitatory

9
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:50.350
transmitter. A field electrode records the field EPSP, the summed excitatory voltage

10
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.910
change from many synapses.

11
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.390
A whole-cell electrode records one neuron directly.

12
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.540
A living slice keeps real circuits intact while letting you control their chemistry.

13
00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:10.280
Glutamate opens AMPA channels, yet slower NMDA pores stay blocked by magnesium at

14
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.480
rest. They also need glycine or D-serine bound.

15
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.540
Depolarization relieves much of the magnesium block, allowing larger current.

16
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.500
A lasting larger response marks long-term potentiation.

17
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:29.543
Now predict something every recording depends on.

18
00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:35.443
In adult brain tissue, the space outside cells is about a fifth of the volume.

19
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:41.423
Four fifths lies inside: one part outside for every four parts inside.

20
00:01:42.663 --> 00:01:47.743
When neurons fire hard and leak potassium, which side changes concentration faster?

21
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:55.217
The outside space.

22
00:01:56.157 --> 00:02:01.337
The same leaked potassium in a quarter of the volume changes concentration four

23
00:02:01.337 --> 00:02:06.097
times as much. And the outside holds little potassium to start.

24
00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:13.317
In seizure-like firing, the outside-to-inside ratio can shift E_K, potassium's pull

25
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.677
on voltage, by tens of millivolts.

26
00:02:16.917 --> 00:02:21.457
Healthy astrocytes must clear potassium, while high-affinity transporters clear

27
00:02:21.457 --> 00:02:22.457
glutamate.

28
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.010
Local circuits also shape every recording.

29
00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.850
Excitatory glutamate pulls voltage up, while the inhibitory transmitter GABA opens

30
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.370
chloride channels pulling near chloride's equilibrium potential.

31
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:44.290
Even in one hippocampus, mossy fibre to CA3 potentiation works differently from CA1.

32
00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:48.443
Slices unlocked how synapses strengthen and weaken.

33
00:02:49.883 --> 00:02:55.183
Long-term potentiation was first measured in rabbits at perforant path to dentate

34
00:02:55.183 --> 00:03:02.243
gyrus. Rat hippocampal slices revealed its mechanism at Schaffer collateral to CA1.

35
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:09.863
Group I metabotropic glutamate receptors like mGluR5 trigger hippocampal long-term

36
00:03:09.863 --> 00:03:11.723
depression lasting hours.

37
00:03:12.543 --> 00:03:16.203
Block protein synthesis, and that weakening does not last.

38
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:24.597
In 1996, Hyejin Kang and Erin Schuman applied growth factor BDNF to hippocampal

39
00:03:24.597 --> 00:03:30.797
slices. Synapses strengthened, even after they cut the slices to separate synapses

40
00:03:30.797 --> 00:03:31.957
from their cell bodies.

41
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:38.197
That effect still depended on protein synthesis, so the new protein was made near

42
00:03:38.197 --> 00:03:44.377
the synapses. Holding living circuits open to experiment lets us test how synapses

43
00:03:44.377 --> 00:03:45.397
truly change.
